{#-
  `send_confirm`: one resolved payment, and a person's answer about it.

  This template may be replaced like any other — reordered, regrouped, reworded,
  with sections dropped. What it cannot do is decide what a control means.
  `data-afpay-decision` *declares* a control; afpay's own runtime, injected at
  the layout's trusted-runtime marker under a nonce a frontend cannot forge, is
  what binds that declaration to the route that sends or refuses the payment.
  A page that declares neither control is a broken override and is reported as
  one, because a question with no answer is worse than no window — and the
  question here is whether to move money.

  `document.plan_id` is the plan afpay will submit if this page is approved.
  What is shown is what is confirmed: the terms come from the stored plan, and
  nothing a template does changes which plan the approval names.
-#}
{% extends "layout.html.j2" %}
{% block panel %}
<section class="quote">
<div class="payment-lead"><p class="payment-amount">{{ document.amount }}<span class="unit">{{ document.unit }}</span></p><p class="payment-destination"><span>to</span> {{ document.to }}</p></div>
<dl class="terms"><div><dt>network fee</dt><dd>{{ document.fee }}<span class="unit">{{ document.unit }}</span></dd></div><div><dt>on-chain memo</dt><dd>{{ document.onchain_memo }}</dd></div></dl>
{% if document.debits %}<dl class="debits">{% for debit in document.debits %}<div><dt>debits</dt><dd>{{ debit.amount }}<span class="unit">{{ debit.token }}</span></dd></div>{% endfor %}</dl>
{% endif %}{% with fields = document.details, class = "details" %}{% include "fields.html.j2" %}{% endwith %}
</section>
<div class="decide">
{% for decision in document.decisions %}<button type="button" class="{{ decision.id }}" data-afpay-decision="{{ decision.id }}">{{ decision.label }}</button>
{% endfor %}<span class="decision-status" data-afpay-decision-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
{% endblock %}
